## Traversals

### Preorder (root → left → right)
```cpp
void pre(TreeNode* root) {
    if (!root) return;
    visit(root);        // process BEFORE children
    pre(root->left);
    pre(root->right);
}
```
- Process a node before its subtrees: cloning a tree, serializing,
  building a tree from the root down.

### Inorder (left → root → right)
```cpp
void in(TreeNode* root) {
    if (!root) return;
    in(root->left);
    visit(root);        // process BETWEEN children
    in(root->right);
}
```
- BSTs: inorder gives nodes in sorted order.
- Validate BST, kth smallest, sorted output.

### Postorder (left → right → root)
```cpp
void post(TreeNode* root) {
    if (!root) return;
    post(root->left);
    post(root->right);
    visit(root);        // process AFTER children
}
```
- A node needs its children's results first: height, deleting a tree,
  subtree sums, anything bottom-up.

### Level order (BFS, level by level)
```cpp
void levelOrder(TreeNode* root) {
    if (!root) return;
    queue<TreeNode*> q;
    q.push(root);
    while (!q.empty()) {
        int sz = q.size();              // nodes in this level
        for (int i = 0; i < sz; i++) {
            TreeNode* node = q.front(); q.pop();
            visit(node);
            if (node->left)  q.push(node->left);
            if (node->right) q.push(node->right);
        }
        // end of one level here
    }
}
```
- Iterative, uses a queue (not recursion).
- Level-by-level needs: shortest path, level averages, right-side view, zigzag.

